      "selector": "/entries/27/usage_note",
      "before": "In a wayfinding context, PERSON + FEET indicates pedestrian movement; it does not by itself assert a crossing location.",
      "after": "All three forms are accepted: move_feet; person_generic + move_feet; person_generic + move_feet + rel_here. For a road sign (WAYFINDING), the creator prefers move_feet. This is not a universal preference for every mode or surface. Movement on foot does not by itself identify a crossing point; crossing is a more specific situation supplied by context. The historical crossing task remains in Corpus and source evidence, not as the general meaning of move_feet."
    },
